{%- comment -%}
  OELNOR 3.0 assets, rendered from snippets/meta-tags.liquid so every page gets
  them in <head> without touching the section files.

  CSS is split by page so a phone only downloads what the page renders:
  - o3.css          every page (palette, header, home and landing sections, popup)
  - o3-pages.css    collection, contact, tracking, policies, ParcelPanel, product
  - o3-product.css  product pages
  Fonts: only the faces the first screen needs are preloaded, so they don't
  compete with the hero photo. Archivo is the body text everywhere; the serif
  is preloaded on pages that open with the editorial hero, Anton elsewhere.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign o3_pages_css = false
  assign o3_product_css = false
  assign o3_editorial_top = false

  case request.page_type
    when 'index'
      assign o3_editorial_top = true
    when 'product'
      assign o3_pages_css = true
      assign o3_product_css = true
    when 'collection', 'policy'
      assign o3_pages_css = true
    when 'page'
      case template.suffix
        when 'about', 'autumn'
          assign o3_editorial_top = true
        when 'contact', 'tracking'
          assign o3_pages_css = true
      endcase
  endcase
  if settings.oelnor_pp_path != blank and request.path contains settings.oelnor_pp_path
    assign o3_pages_css = true
  endif
-%}
{%- if request.page_type == 'index' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The home hero photo is the page's largest paint, but the browser only finds it ~110 KB into the
    HTML, after the CSS and fonts, so it started downloading ~2.7s late on a slow phone. Announce it
    here first. Same files and widths as the o3-ehero section in templates/index.json: if the hero
    image is changed there, change the file names here too (a stale name only wastes the preload).
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign hero_mobile = images['oelnor-hero-editorial-mobile-2k.png']
    assign hero_desktop = images['oelnor-hero-editorial-desktop-2k.png']
  -%}
  {%- if hero_mobile -%}
    <link rel="preload" as="image" fetchpriority="high" media="(max-width: 749px)" imagesizes="100vw" imagesrcset="{{ hero_mobile | image_url: width: 540 }} 540w, {{ hero_mobile | image_url: width: 720 }} 720w, {{ hero_mobile | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w, {{ hero_mobile | image_url: width: 1080 }} 1080w">
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if hero_desktop -%}
    <link rel="preload" as="image" fetchpriority="high" media="(min-width: 750px)" imagesizes="100vw" imagesrcset="{{ hero_desktop | image_url: width: 1000 }} 1000w, {{ hero_desktop | image_url: width: 1400 }} 1400w, {{ hero_desktop | image_url: width: 1800 }} 1800w, {{ hero_desktop | image_url: width: 2200 }} 2200w">
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if request.page_type == 'product' and product.media.first.media_type == 'image' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    13/11/2026: the first gallery photo is the product page's largest paint (LCP), but it sits ~190 KB
    into the HTML, so a phone only started downloading it after the CSS and fonts. Same srcset and
    sizes as the eager image in sections/o3-product.liquid: keep both in step.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign o3_lcp = product.media.first.preview_image -%}
  {%- if product.metafields.oelnor.foto_principal.value != blank -%}{%- assign o3_lcp = product.metafields.oelnor.foto_principal.value.preview_image -%}{%- endif -%}
  <link rel="preload" as="image" fetchpriority="high" imagesizes="(min-width: 990px) 58vw, 100vw" imagesrcset="{{ o3_lcp | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w, {{ o3_lcp | image_url: width: 720 }} 720w, {{ o3_lcp | image_url: width: 960 }} 960w, {{ o3_lcp | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w, {{ o3_lcp | image_url: width: 1400 }} 1400w">
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%}
  The cart drawer's stylesheet loads deferred (media="print" onload), so until it arrives the empty
  <cart-drawer> sat in the page flow and pushed everything ~500px down on slow phones, then the page
  jumped back up (CLS 0.57 in PageSpeed). Keep it out of the flow from the first paint;
  component-cart-drawer.css takes over with the same rules once loaded.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  o3.css only restyles the announcement bar and header when the page has an O3 section
  (body:has(.o3-top)). Cart, search, 404 and the collections list are built from Dawn/older
  sections, so they kept the old light header. These are the same rules, applied on every page.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  cart-drawer.drawer { position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; z-index: 1000; width: 100vw; height: 100%; visibility: hidden; }
  html body .announcement-bar-section .utility-bar, html body .announcement-bar-section .announcement-bar { background: #d9b3a6; color: #3a2d29; border: 0; }
  html body .announcement-bar__message { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #3a2d29; }
  html body .section-header .header-wrapper { background: #3a2d29; color: #f7f0ea; border-bottom: 1.5px solid rgba(247,240,234,.22); --color-foreground: 247, 240, 234; --color-background: 58, 45, 41; --color-link: 247, 240, 234; }
  html body .header__heading-link .h2, html body .header__heading-link { font-family: "O3 Anton", Impact, sans-serif; font-size: 28px; letter-spacing: .02em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #f7f0ea; }
  html body .header__menu-item, html body .header__menu-item span { font-family: "O3 Archivo", Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; font-stretch: 125%; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #f7f0ea; }
  html body .header__icon, html body .header__icon .svg-wrapper { color: #f7f0ea; }
  {%- comment -%}
    Product rails scroll sideways. Cards waiting for their scroll-in reveal sat 24px lower, so each
    card jumped up as it was swiped into view, and that extra 24px also let the rail scroll vertically
    under the finger. Rails keep still: no vertical scroll, no rise-in for their cards.
  {%- endcomment %}
  [data-o3-track] { overflow-y: hidden; }
  html.o3-js .o3 [data-o3-track] > [data-o3-reveal]:not([data-in]) { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
</style>
{%- comment -%}
  13/11/2026: o3.css asks for the fonts as url(o3-archivo.woff2), without the ?v= version that
  asset_url adds, so a versioned preload was a different URL: the phone downloaded each font twice
  (48 KB extra) and the preload never helped. Preload the exact URL the stylesheet uses.
{%- endcomment -%}
<link rel="preload" href="{{ 'o3-archivo.woff2' | asset_url | split: '?' | first }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
{%- if o3_editorial_top -%}
  <link rel="preload" href="{{ 'o3-cormorant-normal.woff2' | asset_url | split: '?' | first }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
{%- else -%}
  <link rel="preload" href="{{ 'o3-anton.woff2' | asset_url | split: '?' | first }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
{%- endif -%}
{{ 'o3.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{%- if o3_pages_css -%}
  {{ 'o3-pages.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if o3_product_css -%}
  {{ 'o3-product.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{%- endif -%}
<script src="{{ 'o3.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
